course: dictionary
lesson: 5786
title: Copycat birds
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can work out a new word from the words around it. «Male lyrebirds are famous mimics that copy the calls of many birds and sometimes human sounds such as camera shutters, car alarms and chainsaws.» The clues are copy, calls and sounds, so a lyrebird is a bird that copies sounds.
explain: Now test your meaning by swapping it into a sentence. «Imagine a bird in the garden that copies your mum's phone ringtone, a car alarm and a camera click: that is a lyrebird.» Put in "a bird that copies sounds" and the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: The word also builds a picture for you. A lyrebird is a large Australian bird that lives on the forest floor, and the male has a long tail shaped like a lyre, an old harp. When you know a word's picture, it is easier to remember.
fact: A lyrebird is a large Australian bird that lives on the forest floor.
fact: The male lyrebird has a long tail shaped like a lyre, which is an old harp.
fact: A «mimic» is a creature that copies sounds, and the lyrebird is famous for being one.
fact: Lyrebirds can copy almost any sound they hear, including camera shutters, car alarms and chainsaws.
fact: The lyrebird is shown on the Australian ten-cent coin.
exercise: What is a lyrebird famous for? | Swimming fast in the sea | Laying its eggs in other birds' nests | *Copying almost any sound it hears | Changing colour in winter
exercise: Where does a lyrebird live? | In a busy city park in Britain | On the tops of tall mountains in Canada | *On the forest floor in Australia | In a desert in Africa
exercise: «Male lyrebirds are famous mimics that copy the calls of many birds.» Find and copy one word that means copies. | famous | male | *copy | calls
test: A lyrebird's tail is shaped like what? | *An old harp, called a lyre | A sailing boat | A bunch of flowers
test: «Imagine a bird in the garden that copies a car alarm and a camera click: that is a lyrebird.» What does this tell you about a lyrebird? | *It copies sounds it hears | It only sings one song | It is a fish that swims in the sea
exam: Which is the best meaning of lyrebird? | A type of car alarm | A small garden bird from Europe that only sings at night | A musical instrument played in churches | *A large Australian bird that lives on the forest floor and copies almost any sound it hears
